  "description": "The closed shapes a proto_version 0.6 peer sends and receives, frozen here as 0.7 adds to them: every message below is what a 0.6 core or worker writes and stays valid under 0.7, because every addition is optional or a new message (V1). A connect names a key or a password and carries no `login_timeout`; `auth_failed` carries no `code`; `open_shell` carries `open_timeout`; the handshake is at 0.6. The core speaks 0.7 and 0.6 and sends a 0.6 worker exactly these messages, none of the device-login ones. Two cases stay refused: an `open_timeout` of 0, and a credential on a telnet connect.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §6.4",
    "device-login, V1",
    "ipc-control version paragraph"
  ],
